(A thing's list field handed back by `Return a value` or `Return a list` is
 the caller's own copy: the thing keeps its field.)
A thing called note has
  a list called items.

a note called memo.
append "a" to memo's items.

To 'give as a value'.
    Return a value, memo's items.

To 'give as a list'.
    Return a list, memo's items.

a value called boxed is 'give as a value'.
a list called listed is 'give as a list'.
Free memo's items.
Print "boxed: {boxed}".
append "z" to listed.
Print "listed: {listed}, memo: {memo's items}".
